      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 6392201955886577111, guid: 7dc5e6bd30240a74db319824c2c30e9b, type: 3}
      propertyPath: TempSoundscapes.Array.data[1].group
      value: 
      objectReference: {fileID: 4996366648319053103, guid: cd56ee2d263c9e64eadcc5bcb87af9e5, type: 2}
    - target: {fileID: 6392201955886577111, guid: 7dc5e6bd30240a74db319824c2c30e9b, type: 3}
      propertyPath: TempSoundscapes.Array.data[21].text
      value: 'Decrypt: This is a test dev commentary.'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 6392201955886577111, guid: 7dc5e6bd30240a74db319824c2c30e9b, type: 3}
      propertyPath: TempSoundscapes.Array.data[22].text
      value: 'Decrypt: Welcome to Fractal, it''s Decrypt. Lead developer of the game.
        These comments will help you learn the dev process behind the  game development
        and also learn some tricks of it''s design. Also to clarify, if you want
        to listen to the nodes, just interact with them the exact way you did with
        this one.'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 6392201955886577111, guid: 7dc5e6bd30240a74db319824c2c30e9b, type: 3}
      propertyPath: TempSoundscapes.Array.data[23].text
      value: 'Decrypt: This is the most hated chamber of mine. I can say that I spent
        entire 6 months in this very chamber.  Yes, this chamber was a testground
        for almost every testing element and mechanic of the game and also it is
        the only chamber that is not made of many meshes, rather one big mesh. In
        the beginning I wanted to do it that way, but decided to stick to building
        it in unity instead of blender, due to ability to edit it without changing
        the model in blender.  But yeah, this chamber brings back not the best memories.'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 6392201955886577111, guid: 7dc5e6bd30240a74db319824c2c30e9b, type: 3}
      propertyPath: TempSoundscapes.Array.data[24].text
      value: 'Decrypt: In game development you usually add details only to the parts
        player can actually see.  There is no point of detailing the parts that cannot
        be seen and that would load the engine a bit more, which you dont really
        want.  And this chamber is an example of it. You see, this "behind the scenes"
        view is only detailed from the side you can actually see it, and if you look
        at the different angle, you will see that the walls are not connected at
        all, and overall its not looking good.'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 6392201955886577111, guid: 7dc5e6bd30240a74db319824c2c30e9b, type: 3}
      propertyPath: TempSoundscapes.Array.data[25].text
      value: 'Decrypt: And this is the first chamber to include mirrors. The fun
        thing is that reflections of these mirrors were the late addition because
        I felt that they are not really needed and would make the game laggy and
        unplayable, but they turned out really nice and I''m happy that people pointed
        lack of reflections which kind of forced me to revisit these.'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 6392201955886577111, guid: 7dc5e6bd30240a74db319824c2c30e9b, type: 3}
      propertyPath: TempSoundscapes.Array.data[26].text
      value: '[Distant explosion]'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
